cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZMART Analysis: reproducible, environment-isolated image analysis pipelines for live adaptive microscopy"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: de Hoog
    given-names: Thom
    affiliation: "Center for Microscopy and Image Analysis (ZMB), University of Zurich"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thomdehoog/ZMART-analysis"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - microscopy
  - image-analysis
  - bioimage-analysis
  - pipeline
  - cellpose
  - python
  - conda
  - live-acquisition
  - smart-microscopy
abstract: >-
  The analysis half of ZMART, the microscopy toolkit of the Center for
  Microscopy and Image Analysis (ZMB), University of Zurich. Pipelines are
  YAML recipes of small Python steps; each step runs in its own conda
  environment inside a worker that stays warm, so analysis keeps pace with
  a microscope that is still acquiring, and steps can be scoped to run once
  per field, per well or per plate. Ships workflows for focus scoring,
  object detection and measurement, population plots and driver
  configuration.
